TEST 13553 -- QoS: switchport interface - wrr weightings applied
===========================================================================
Run: 2026-09-22, tb470

VERDICT: UNMEASURED -- requires congestion this bench cannot create.

The case's own method: "Use 2 x 1gig input to egress a single 1 gig port, to
create congestion. 1 ingress stream set to use particular egress queue. 2nd
egress stream to use a different queue."

Strict-priority queueing is only OBSERVABLE under congestion -- with an
uncongested egress every queue drains and all streams pass, so the scheduler's
priority order has no effect to measure. Creating congestion needs TWO 1 Gbps
ingress streams converging on one 1 Gbps egress.

This bench has ONE usable ingress port. Each IE520-28GSX member has exactly
one copper port: port1.0.2 is the egress (to the x230), port2.0.2 is the
ingress, port3.0.2 has no cable, port4.0.2 is the LAG to the AR4050S. There is
no second cabled ingress, and scapy from a single host peaks at ~26 Mbps in
this harness -- 2.5% of what is needed to congest a gigabit port.

TO CLOSE: a second cabled ingress port and a line-rate traffic source.
Both are bench-access items. The default queueing configuration itself can be
read with `show mls qos interface <port>` without traffic, but that shows
configuration, not behaviour, and is not what the case asks for.

CASE-SPECIFIC NOTE: this case asks that "the output should reflect the ratio of
wrr weightings". A ratio between queues can only appear when the queues are
backlogged, i.e. under the same congestion T13549 needs. Identical blocker.
